CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* friend of derived class: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
clang++ rejects it, contrary to N5008 [class.access.base]/4.3 (see
main.cpp); there is no clang harness check for this test.
